# (key: heads-first) THE HEADS-FIRST CERTIFICATE of the cross-replica hosted network (lg-g2 blocker B1)

`XNetW.heads_first`: for p-a3's network `N` and a set `hb` of A4 host bins that are never hosted and whose remaining
climb is 48, with head directions `z` such that the head block takes the A4 start frame to the end frame up to a free
step (`hz`), there is a proper word `body` with
* `GLiveKernel Sum.inl (MX.headWord Sum.inl (headsL hb) (fun _ => 48) z ind ++ body)` (the input of e-r45m1's
  `MX.cut_heads_half`, with `a = b = 24`): ONE block of rank 48 on each head role, all of them FIRST;
* price `card Γ * N.unit φ - |headsL hb| * φ 48` for every price list `φ` (the network's, less the heads).
Route (a) of the p-hfirst brief: the heads are an explicit prefix, the body is the network `N.toHF` (Work/XHostT/HF/
ToHF.lean), whose certificate with a prefix is `XNetHW.cert_pre` (Work/XHostT/HF/Cert.lean).
Written by p-hfirst (wht45/lever, 19 Oct 2026); prepared with assistance from Claude.  No `sorry`.
WARP variant (Heads): generated by x-inst/tools/mk_hfw2979.py (wht45/lever2979, 19 Oct 2026) from
p-hfirst's file of the same name (sha256 pinned in tools/hfw2979-inputs.sha256), with p-a3's mk_warp.py
substitutions (providers `GInvW .. Ok`, window facts `hok0 .. hok8`, stages `gistageW_fwd/bwd`).
